title: >
  OnTEPT: A Multimodal OWL 2 DL Ontology for the Automated
  Identification of Post-Traumatic Stress Disorder

authors:
  - family-names: "[Apellido]"
    given-names: "Alejandro"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX"
    affiliation: >
      Universidad de Nariño, Facultad de Ingeniería,
      Pasto, Nariño, Colombia

version: "1.0"
date-released: "2025-XX-XX"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX"
url: "https://github.com/TU_USUARIO/onTEPT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/TU_USUARIO/onTEPT"
license: CC-BY-4.0

abstract: >
  OnTEPT is an OWL 2 DL ontology that integrates the diagnostic
  criteria of DSM-5 and ICD-11 for post-traumatic stress disorder
  (PTSD), three psychometric instruments (PCL-5, CAPS-5,
  PC-PTSD-5), and electroencephalographic (EEG) features into a
  single formal knowledge representation. The ontology enables
  automated patient classification through OWL reasoning, formal
  interoperability between DSM-5 and ICD-11, explicit item-to-
  criterion mappings via the evaluatesSymptomCluster annotation
  property, and logical inconsistency detection. OnTEPT was
  developed and validated with real and synthetic patient data
  at the Universidad de Nariño, Colombia.

keywords:
  - ontology
